---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Manifesto — Maxxtopia"
  description="Why Maxxtopia exists. The principles behind the suite."
>
  <article class="relative">
    <div class="ambient-glow" style="opacity: 0.4"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 sm:px-8 pt-24 pb-12">
      <p class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-[var(--color-subtle)] font-mono">
        Manifesto · v0.1
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[44px] sm:text-[60px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-[1] gradient-text">
        We're tired of bad gaming software.
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 sm:px-8 pb-32">
      <div class="space-y-7 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.75] text-[var(--color-muted)]">
        <p>
          The tools competitive gamers actually use weren't built by anyone competitive.
          They were built by Discord scripters who slapped a paywall on a registry batch file,
          by Electron studios shipping 200 MB of Chromium for a settings panel,
          by analytics-funded SaaS that treats your inputs as inventory.
        </p>

        <p>
          Maxxtopia is a refusal to accept that.
          We think gaming utilities should be designed with the care Apple gives a music app.
          That a tuner should cite its sources. That a Discord client should idle at 0% CPU.
          That a clip tool should measure what actually goes viral, not just spike on volume.
          That nothing in your gaming stack should call home unless you tell it to.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-tight pt-6 leading-tight">
          Principles
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-5">
          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] pl-5">
            <h3 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[18px] font-semibold mb-1.5">Sourced, not vibed.</h3>
            <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7]">
              Every tweak we ship traces to Microsoft Learn, a vendor doc, or a verified community source.
              If it can't be cited, it doesn't ship. Placebo tweaks erode trust — we cut ten of them in v0.1.32.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] pl-5">
            <h3 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[18px] font-semibold mb-1.5">Native or nothing.</h3>
            <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7]">
              The tuner is 3.6 MB. The Discord client is 288 MB at idle versus 1041 MB on stock.
              Bundle size is a moral position.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] pl-5">
            <h3 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[18px] font-semibold mb-1.5">Reversible by default.</h3>
            <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7]">
              Every change is snapshot-backed. Every preset is undoable. One-click restore.
              Software you can experiment with because the door is never locked.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] pl-5">
            <h3 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[18px] font-semibold mb-1.5">No telemetry. Ever.</h3>
            <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7]">
              We don't analytics you. We don't error-log you. We don't &ldquo;help us improve our product&rdquo; you.
              Gaming software has a long history of betraying that trust. We won't.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] pl-5">
            <h3 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[18px] font-semibold mb-1.5">Measure, don't just modify.</h3>
            <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7]">
              Every tuner applies tweaks. Maxxtopia&apos;s ships live DPC graphs, latency probes, and PCIe diagnostics
              so you can verify the change worked. Trust, then verify.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-[var(--color-text)] text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-tight pt-6 leading-tight">
          The suite
        </h2>

        <p>
          Optimizationmaxxing tunes your PC.
          Discordmaxxer tunes your comms.
          Clipmaxxer cuts your VODs.
          Dropmaxxer picks your spots.
          Aimmaxxer drills your gap.
          Viewmaxxing handles your stream.
          Editmacros assists your edits.
        </p>

        <p>
          Different surfaces. Same standard.
          Built by a single player for the players who care about the millisecond.
        </p>

        <p class="pt-4 text-[var(--color-text)] font-mono text-[14px]">
          — The Maxxtopia team
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-[var(--color-line)]">
        <a href="/#suite" class="btn-primary">
          Browse the suite
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
